# scenario 06.1: Status shows where each increment stands
# Increment 07 has its test, a passed manual scenario, a review result with
# only a note, and a retro: done. Increment 08 has a test for 08.1 only: it
# waits for tests and names 08.2. Increment 09 has its test and a review
# result, but no result for its demonstrated scenario and no retro: it
# waits for results and names both.
env GIT_AUTHOR_NAME=Agent GIT_AUTHOR_EMAIL=agent@example.com GIT_COMMITTER_NAME=Agent GIT_COMMITTER_EMAIL=agent@example.com
cd repo
exec git init -q -b main
exec git add -A
exec git commit -q -m base

exec factory status
stdout '(?s)^status: 07-sample done\n.*^status: 08-later tests\n.*^status: 09-third results\n'
stdout '^status: 08-later missing-test 08\.2$'
! stdout 'missing-test 08\.1'
stdout '^status: 09-third waits-for-engineer 09\.2 demonstrated$'
stdout '^status: 09-third missing-retro$'
! stdout '^status: 07-sample (missing-test|missing-review|blocking-review|waits-for-engineer|failed|missing-retro)'
! stdout '^status: 09-third (missing-test|missing-review|blocking-review|failed)'
stdout '^status: ok 3 checked$'
! stdout ': error '

-- repo/README.md --
# Sample
-- repo/internal/x.go --
package x
-- repo/.factory/code-paths --
internal/**
-- repo/docs/increments/07-sample/design.md --
# Increment 07: sample

## Goal

- The sample tool of increment 07 works.

## Out of scope

- Everything else.

## Existing tools

- None found; searched for sample tools.

## Interface

- `sample run`

## Rollout

- Off switch: none. Failure signal: the tool rejects a correct input.

## Evidence

- Approved scenarios: 07.1.

## Scenarios

- **scenario 07.1** (automated) **A sample thing works.** Given a sample thing, the tool accepts it.
- **scenario 07.2** (manual) **A person checks the sample.** Given a sample thing, the tool accepts it.
